<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Scenario catalog strings, English.

  Every key here is referenced by name at runtime from `org.jaagruk.core.catalog.ModuleCatalog`, not through
  `R.string`. The list is generated by `./gradlew :core:dumpCatalogManifest` and audited on every debug launch,
  so a scenario option added in `:core` without a translation is caught in the build rather than by a worker
  looking at a blank button.

  Content rules, and they matter more than the wording:

    * Distractors are plausible, not silly. "Fight the fire first" and "find your supervisor" are what people
      actually do wrong. A test whose wrong answers are obviously wrong measures nothing.
    * Remediation says what to do, not that the answer was wrong. It is the one thing a worker takes away.
    * Statutory content follows the Mines Act 1952, the Mines Rules 1955, DGMS circulars and the Factories Act
      1948 as they apply to Jharkhand coal, steel and mica operations.
-->
